  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving protection and educational services to South Sudanese refugees in Nguenyviel, Kule and Pugnido refugee camps in the Gambella region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Older people&apos;s protection and inclusion services enhanced to support their wellbeing and dignity in Kule and Nguenyyiel</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Lifesaving protection and education services to South Sudanese refugees in Nguenyyiel, Kule and Pinyudo refugee camps in Gambella Region project was awarded to Plan International. The goal of the project is strengthen the protective environment for refugees and host communities through improved access to quality and equitable education and provision of appropriate protection services to children and persons with specific needs, including elderly persons and persons living with disabilities, in Nguenyyiel, Kule, and Pinyudo refugee camps in Gambella Region. Building on the experience of Plan&apos;s previous PRM-funded Gambella region project, this project expands the sectoral reach to address the protection needs of older adults and PwDs. The project&apos;s protection activities will directly complement its child protection interventions, as there is considerable overlap in the vulnerabilities experienced by children and older adults. This approach is based on Plan&apos;s long-term experience in all three camps, and will result in holistic, impactful programming. To achieve this, Plan has partnered with HelpAge International and RaDO to expand the program&apos;s sectoral expertise as well as geographic reach. Plan will be responsible for activity implementation under Objectives 1 and 2 in all three camps, as well as overall consortium coordination and oversight. HelpAge will be responsible for implementation of Objective 3 activities in Kule and Nguenyyiel, and RaDO will be responsible for Objective 3 activities in Pinyudo.</narrative>
  </description>
